      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Problem: Check if a Number is a Neon Number\n\nGiven an integer N, determine whether it is a Neon number.\n\nA Neon number is a number whose sum of the digits of its square is equal to the number itself.\n\nReturn \"Yes\" if N is a Neon number; otherwise, return \"No\".\n\nExamples:\nInput: 9\nOutput: Yes\nExplanation: 9² = 81, and 8 + 1 = 9.\n\nInput: 10\nOutput: No\nExplanation: 10² = 100, and 1 + 0 + 0 = 1 ≠ 10.\n\nConstraints:\n0 ≤ N ≤ 10⁶",
      "fontSize": 53.14084147217758,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Problem: Check if a Number is a Neon Number\n\nGiven an integer N, determine whether it is a Neon number.\n\nA Neon number is a number whose sum of the digits of its square is equal to the number itself.\n\nReturn \"Yes\" if N is a Neon number; otherwise, return \"No\".\n\nExamples:\nInput: 9\nOutput: Yes\nExplanation: 9² = 81, and 8 + 1 = 9.\n\nInput: 10\nOutput: No\nExplanation: 10² = 100, and 1 + 0 + 0 = 1 ≠ 10.\n\nConstraints:\n0 ≤ N ≤ 10⁶",
